0..72 Comment "/// This source states the degree `ξ` of a pointed map of the 3-sphere."
73..76 Comment "///"
77..150 Comment "/// The degree is the winding of the image of the 3-cell. Each later rung"
151..223 Comment "/// applies `xi` to its own map. The checker converts each degree to its"
224..275 Comment "/// integer, and the kernel replays the conversion."
276..279 Comment "///"
280..353 Comment "/// `wind3` cases on the words at the 3-cell, as `wind` cases on the loop"
354..432 Comment "/// words of the circle. Its `here` arm reads its words from the type that the"
433..509 Comment "/// scrutinee\'s position states. `xi` reads a pointed map as a map `f` and a"
510..581 Comment "/// path `p` from `f Base3` to `Base3`. The transport along `p` carries"
582..655 Comment "/// `Path.ap f surf3` to the 3-cells at the point. The kernel checks each"
656..706 Comment "/// layer of `Path.ap f surf3` against the 3-cell."
707..710 Comment "///"
711..791 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/sphere-maps.gandr — `sphereId3`, the identity"
792..822 Comment "///   of the 3-sphere by cases"
823..900 Comment "/// - see: corpus/model/identity/circle-base.gandr — `wind`, the winding at"
901..920 Comment "///   dimension one"
922..955 Comment "// The 2-sphere and the 3-sphere."
